<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Yanzheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 951</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Yanzheng was the last ruler of the Min kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/five-dynasties-and-ten-kingdoms-period">Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms period</a>. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-shenzhi">Wang Shenzhi</a>, he rebelled against his brother, the emperor Wang Yanxi, and in 943 proclaimed his own state, Yin, at Jianzhou. After Wang Yanxi was murdered in 944 he claimed the Min throne, but in 945 the Southern Tang conquered his realm and took him captive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-yanzheng.jpg" alt="Wang Yanzheng" width="307" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author in Ming Dynasty (1368-1644) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wang_Yanzheng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
